{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1176591-what-purview-both-old-and-new-would-be-able-to-cause-psychosomatic-injuries","id":1176591,"title":"What Purview Both Old and New Would Be Able to Cause Psychosomatic Injuries?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-16T13:54:52-08:00","id":1176591,"title":"What Purview Both Old and New Would Be Able to Cause Psychosomatic Injuries?","content":"What purviews would be considered to legitimately inflict psychosomatic injuries and conditions? And has anybody done this in the past?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13647-manannansun","name":"Manannansun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T14:39:29-08:00","id":1176605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manannansun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1176591-what-purview-both-old-and-new-would-be-able-to-cause-psychosomatic-injuries#post1176591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What purviews would be considered to legitimately inflict psychosomatic injuries and conditions? And has anybody done this in the past?</div> </div> </div> </div>By 'Old Purviews' and 'New Purviews' I assume you mean the Purviews of 1e and 2e Manannansun?<br /> <br /> In both editions, from what we know of 2e, I would probably purely limit it to Moon or Epic Manipulation / Illusion / Deception (I think?). It very much depends on the flavor of how it is all working.<br /> <br /> Moon is the Purview that interacts with the Mythic conceptualization of Madness (not the Medical concept of Mental Illness, I always differentiate them in my games since they tend to be really different) so Moon should be able to interact with such things. If you want to actually inflict a Psychosomatic injury or illness on another, that would be solidly in the realm of Moon. A Scion touched by Selene's amorous gravity might be able to reach out, and inflict a 'Curse' upon another where they believed that they had lost a limb for example.<br /> <br /> If, on the other hand, a Scion of Fand was using the powers of the Otherworld to dupe, deceive, and confuse another person into believing that they were wounded or being eaten by horses for example, that would be Illusion, or Deception (If Deception will work the way I think it will). Illusion lets you alter the perceptions of another being in a more material way, you are enchanting them, confusing them, but not something as corporeal as laying a touch of Lunacy upon them. In this case, it wouldn't <i>actually</i> be a Psychosomatic injury in the same way that Illusion doesn't make people schizophrenic, it just duplicates the effects.<br /> <br /> If for a third option, someone with Epic Manipulation might be able to gaslight someone into believing they had an injury or condition they did not have. This one would either take a lot of time, or to be very high Legend to pull off easily though. Mortals can be utterly horrific to each other and convince each other of things through years of psychological abuse, but to duplicate such effects with a snap of your fingers would probably require mid to high Demigod Epic Manipulation if contesting against a mortal, let alone someone of some divine mental fortitude.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's ever come up in one of our games. People have been hurt in visions, but nothing quite psychosomatic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T16:04:46-08:00","id":1176622,"title":"","content":"By injury do you mean like cause physical damage with them? If so I think the above answer works, although I'd through in Chaos and Darkness if those are still around, but I'd also add I'd be kinda hesitant to let something like that exist in the first place as it brings in the usual questions. Kinda easy to get cheesy with those sorts of powers mainly.<br /> For mechanical conditions, again everything above, but also Passion. That one seems pretty obvious to me, since it can apparently include any type of emotion such as fear, dread, angst, sorrow, and so on. Also perhaps negative uses of Beauty, which is I think I new one that was added on recently in one of the pantheon previews.<br /> And if by conditions you mean just RP stuff instead of the conditions listed in the preview, well technically speaking any old purview could do that. I have to imagine horribly mutilating someone with fire would make them scared for fire for instance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3109-lionmanguy","name":"Lionmanguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}